==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Wargod Kenshin''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Immortal Kenshin''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

Evolves into '''Hellrider Kenshin''' at level 60 using [[Catfruit]], [[Catfruit#Behemoth Stones|Behemoth Stones]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
This Uber has great DPS, especially against Dark enemies; despite this, she cannot be safely used against Dark backliners like [[Le'noir]] due to her range. In addition, she also has great speed, damage and health so she can be a great aid in early game.

Her knockback effect against Darks is more useful than [[Date Masamune (Uber Rare Cat)|Date Masamune]]'s, due to her fast attacks, guaranteed effect chance and damage amplifier. She can perma-knockback [[Razorback]] as long as she is guarded by a decent amount of meatshields.

She is a part of the [[Hecks Angels (Combo)|Hecks Angels]] [[Cat Combo|Combo]], which is great for beating easy stages really fast or [[Cheese|cheesing]] [[hitbox]] glitch levels.

==='''True Form'''===
Immortal Kenshin is tougher and faster in both movement and attacks, with increased DPS as a result. These improvements change nearly nothing in how she is used, she is just better in every way and can stand up to more enemies and situations.

==='''Ultra Form'''===
Kenshin's largest gains by far is the level 4 [[Wave Attack|Mini-Wave]] ability. While it can deal some chip damage, it primarily serves as an extension to Kenshin's Knockback ability against her targeted traits, pushing anything evading the initial hit for extra mayhem, and may even reach those she struggles to reach normally, such as [[Golem Sunfish]] or [[Director Kurosawah]]. The stat and range increases are obviously noteworthy, making her more comfortable to use. The recharge reduction doesn't change her as much by contrast due to merely shaving ten seconds or so from the timer.

One notable usage case for her is in [[Rank-Up Test 3 (Rank 12)]], one of the most difficult stages in the game. With her new Mini-Wave she is able to permanently Knockback [[Masked Okame|Okame]], removing a major threat from the stage. Furthermore with [[Talents]] she can also target Relic and become Immune to Curse, which allows her to counter one of the other major threats in the stage, [[Ancient Magamojoe]].

==='''Talents'''===
Health and damage are good to have, especially for a unit that relies on her stats like Kenshin, but nothing groundbreaking. Things get interesting with the Target Relic and Curse Immune talents, however.

Immortal Kenshin, as an anti-Relic, has a lot of value, becoming a near perfect counter to [[Oldhorn]] while also having good enough damage and attack rate to easily deal with any relic peons that may get in her way. Keep in mind that a speedy unit with a knockback ability may not always be beneficial to a fight, so, especially if dealing with the likes of [[M. Ost]] or [[Lowkey]], it is best to think twice before using her. If her Ultra Form is unlocked, however, then the backliner issue is somewhat nullified due to her Mini-Wave.

Resist Weaken is way too situational to be worth the NP, especially since so few Dark or Relic enemies can weaken in the first place.

{{Job|Classification = Backliner & Crowd-Controller}}

