==Trivia==
*Prior to [[Version 4.7 Update|Version 4.7]], Uesugi Kenshin was a part of another [[Cat Combo]] called [[Nemeses (Removed Combo)|Nemeses]].
*Prior to [[Version 15.4 Update|Version 15.4]], Uesugi Kenshin's descriptions read as follows:
<pre>Uesugi Kenshin
Transformed into a dragon through the cursed
magic of the Nyanko Engine. (Area attack)
Strong + 100% Knockback against Dark.</pre>
<pre>Wargod Kenshin
Deciding to fully fuse with the Nyanko Engine,
the great general gave in to darkness. (Area att.)
Strong + 100% Knockback against Dark.</pre>
<pre>Immortal Kenshin
Totally consumed by corruption. The only emotion
remaining is the will to destruction. (Area Attacks)
Strong + 100% Knockback against Dark.</pre>
**Immortal Kenshin's Pre-15.4 descriptions contained a typo, in that "cause" was missing from the second line.
*Uesugi Kenshin's Normal and Evolved Form descriptions both reference her Area Attack ability twice.
*This was the first [[Sengoku Wargods Vajiras (Gacha Event)|Sengoku Wargod]] to have a seasonal [[Springtime Kenshin (Uber Rare Cat)|variant]].
*Uesugi Kenshin is normally portrayed as male in some media, but they are also equally portrayed as female. This is largely due to the fact that in real life Uesugi's gender is often debated, with valid arguments for both genders often leaving historians puzzled.
*Uesugi Kenshin is known for having rivalry with Takeda Shingen during the Sengoku Period. Uesugi Kenshin also had conflicts with other warlords such as Oda Nobunaga.
*The kanji on one of the claws is the first letter in "毘沙門天". This reads "Bishamonten" and is the Japanese name for the Buddhist deity Vaiśravana. As a devotee to Bishamonten, Uesugi Kenshin used the character "毘" on her battle flags.

